<title>UK: Baltic Freight Index rose to 1,465.</title>
<headline>Baltic Freight Index rose to 1,465.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic Freight Index for spot dry cargo shipping rates rose to 1,465 today from 1,460 on Feb 14, with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals</p>
<p>1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates</p>
<p>in dollars per tonne.</p>
<p> Route Index     Rate   Prev Index  Rate</p>
<p>   1    1568    14.231	  1554    14.106</p>
<p>   1a   1499 11350.000	  1503 11381.000</p>
<p>   2    1861    26.588	  1851    26.438</p>
<p>   2a   1874 15369.000	  1869 15331.000</p>
<p>   3    1599    14.750	  1578    14.563</p>
<p>   3a   1510 11919.000	  1510 11919.000</p>
<p>   6    1242    12.806	  1245    12.844</p>
<p>   7    1176     5.725	  1186     5.775</p>
<p>   8     897     9.863	   901     9.906</p>
<p>   9     814  7119.000	   793  6938.000</p>
<p>  10    1119     5.650	  1126     5.688</p>
